//bruteforce
**Time Complexity (TC): O(N²)**

- The outer loop runs N times.
- For each iteration of the outer loop, the inner loop can run up to N times.
- Counting zeros and updating the answer take O(1) time per iteration.

Therefore, TC = O(N × N) = **O(N²)**.

**Space Complexity (SC): O(1)**

- Only a few extra variables are used: `n`, `ans`, `zerocnt`, `i` and `j`.
- No additional data structure is used.

Therefore, SC = **O(1)**.

class Solution {
public:
    int longestOnes(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.size();
        int ans = INT_MIN;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int zerocnt = 0;
            for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
                if(nums[j] == 0)
                {
                    zerocnt++;
                }
                if(zerocnt <= k)
                {
                    ans = max(ans,j - i + 1);
                }
            }
        }
        if(ans == INT_MIN)
        {
            return 0;
        }
        return ans;
    }
};

//optimal
**Time Complexity (TC): O(N)**

- The `tail` pointer traverses the array at most N times.
- The `head` pointer also traverses the array at most N times.
- Although there is a nested `while` loop, `head` never moves backward.
- Each element is added to and removed from the window at most once.

Therefore, TC = O(N + N) = **O(N)**.

**Space Complexity (SC): O(1)**

- Only a constant number of variables are used: `n`, `ans`, `head`, `tail` and `zerocnt`.
- No additional data structure is used.

Therefore, SC = **O(1)**.

**Approach:** Sliding Window / Two Pointers.

class Solution {
public:
    int longestOnes(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.size();
        int ans = INT_MIN;

        int head = -1;
        int tail = 0;
   
        int zerocnt = 0;
        while(tail < n)
        {
            while(head + 1 < n && (zerocnt < k || zerocnt == k && nums[head + 1] == 1))
            {
                head++;
                if(nums[head] == 0)
                {
                    zerocnt++;
                }
            }
             ans = max(ans,head - tail + 1);
            

            if(tail <= head)
            {
                if(nums[tail] == 0)
                {
                    zerocnt--;
                   
                }
                 tail++;
                
            }
            else
            {
                tail++;
                head = tail - 1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
};

